Verification controls confirm that security actually works — through the four complementary types of security testing defined in IEC 62443-4-1: security requirements testing, risk mitigation testing, vulnerability identification testing, and penetration testing. Design and implementation intentions are only as good as the evidence that they work. These controls provide that evidence and catch defects before they reach users.

